# =============================================================================
# Trivy scan exceptions — JUSTIFIED, TIME-WINDOWED only.   (policy: Phase 226)
# =============================================================================
#
# HOW THIS WORKS
#   `make scan` passes each finding listed here to Trivy's --ignorefile, so a
#   listed CVE no longer fails the gate UNTIL its `exp:` date, after which Trivy
#   stops ignoring it and the scan fails again — forcing a re-review.
#   Run `make scan-exceptions` to list every entry with days-remaining.
#
# RULES (enforced by review, surfaced by `make scan-exceptions`)
#   1. NO blanket ignores. One entry per CVE, only when there is genuinely no
#      fix available (anything fixable is patched via apt/apk upgrade instead).
#   2. Every entry MUST have:
#        - a comment block (lines starting with '#') directly above it stating
#          WHY there is no fix and WHY it is not exploitable in our images;
#        - an inline expiry: `CVE-XXXX-NNNNN exp:YYYY-MM-DD`.
#   3. Maximum window is 14 days. Pick exp: = today + 14d so exceptions are
#      re-justified often and never quietly become permanent.
#
# OPERATOR: ADD / EDIT / DELETE
#   ADD    — append a '#' comment block (why no-fix + why safe) then the
#            `CVE-... exp:<today+14d>` line.
#   EDIT   — change the `exp:` date (re-justify in the comment) when extending.
#   DELETE — remove the comment block + the CVE line once a fix is available
#            (and rely on apt/apk upgrade to clear it) or the risk is resolved.
#   Verify with `make scan-exceptions` (warns on expired / soon-to-expire).
# =============================================================================

# CVE-2026-42496 (CRITICAL) / CVE-2026-42497 (HIGH) — perl-archive-tar path
# traversal (Archive::Tar < 3.08) in perl-base on python:3.14-slim (analytics,
# tarpit). No fix: Debian trixie marks it fix_deferred (no patched package).
# Not exploitable here: our services are Python/Go and never invoke Archive::Tar
# on untrusted input; perl-base is only a transitive base package.
# Real fix: Phase 229 (perl-free base). Re-review at expiry.
CVE-2026-42496 exp:2026-06-20
CVE-2026-42497 exp:2026-06-20

# CVE-2026-8376 (CRITICAL) — Perl interpreter heap buffer overflow (Perl
# <= 5.43.10) in perl-base on python:3.14-slim (analytics, tarpit). No fix:
# Debian marks perl-base `affected` with no fixed version. Not exploitable here:
# we never execute the perl interpreter on untrusted input. Real fix: Phase 229.
CVE-2026-8376 exp:2026-06-20
